# nr-relay-feedback-http: wire lines for mixdog-relay (src/feedback/http.rs, src/feedback/mailer.rs)

No protocol method is added; nothing is registered in a hot file; SERVICE_PENDING loses no name.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml

After the `[[test]]` block of `feedback_service` add:

    [[test]]
    name = "feedback_http"
    path = "tests/feedback_http.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

No dependency is added. The code uses mixdog-js, mixdog-rt, serde_json and tokio (rt, macros: `select!`) that the manifest lists;
the tests use rcgen, rustls, tokio-rustls, tempfile, base64 and mixdog-fsio, all already in [dependencies] or [dev-dependencies]. Cargo.lock and the
workspace hack need nothing.

## What nr-relay-server / ingress connects (all in `mixdog_relay::feedback`)

- Build: `let mailer = Mailer::from_env(&config.env);` (None unless SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASSWORD are set), then
  `let options = match &mailer { Some(m) => m.options(FeedbackOptions::default()), None => FeedbackOptions::default() };` and
  `FeedbackService::start(&data_dir, durability_io, mailer.map(|m| Arc::new(m) as Arc<dyn FeedbackSender>), options).await`.
  `Mailer::options` sets `From` = SMTP_USER and `To` = FEEDBACK_TO (default support@mixdog.ai); the SMTP timeout is the 15 s of `MailConfig`.
- Route: `FeedbackEndpoint::new(Some(service))` (`None` when the service failed to build), held in an `Arc`; for a request whose
  path before `?` is `/feedback` spawn `endpoint.handle(request, response)` and finish a failure with `http1::fail_request("feedback", ..)`
  (`server.mjs`: `handleFeedbackRequest(...).catch(failRequest(request, response, 'feedback'))`).
- Close: `endpoint.service()` gives the service whose `close().await` the relay calls (`closeRelay`, `finishRelayStart`).
- The 60 s body timeout is `feedback::http::BODY_TIMEOUT`; `with_body_timeout` exists for tests only to shorten it.
